---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import ProcessSteps from '../components/ProcessSteps.astro';
import ServiceArea from '../components/ServiceArea.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../components/ComparisonTable.astro';
import NetworkDiagram from '../components/NetworkDiagram.astro';
import WirelessBridgeDiagram from '../components/WirelessBridgeDiagram.astro';
import WifiDiagram from '../components/WifiDiagram.astro';
import { faqs } from '../config/faqs';
import { breadcrumbNode, faqNode } from '../config/schema';

const description =
	'Websites, UniFi networks, security cameras, EV charging, and Lutron automation for Colorado homes and businesses. Technology you own and control.';

const extraSchema = [
	faqNode(faqs.home),
	breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Home"
	fullTitle="Meridian Integrations | Colorado Technology Integration"
	description={description}
	extraSchema={extraSchema}
>
	<Hero />

	<section class="trust" aria-label="Disciplines">
		<div class="wrap trust-row">
			<p class="trust-line">Digital. Network. Energy. Automation.</p>
			<p class="trust-note">Technology designed around the way you live and work — and kept in your control.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="services" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<h2 id="services-heading">Invisible Technology. Flawless Aesthetics.</h2>
				</div>
				<p class="lede">
					Meridian Integrations engineers high-performance networking, structural security,
					and automation infrastructure designed to vanish into your architecture. 
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="quad lift">
				<a class="service-card" href="/website-solutions/">
					<span class="card-index">Digital</span>
					<h3>Website &amp; cloud infrastructure</h3>
					<p>
						Fast, secure business websites on GitHub and Cloudflare, with the source code in your hands and no
						traditional monthly hosting fee for qualifying static sites.
					</p>
					<span class="card-cta">Website Solutions</span>
				</a>
				<a class="service-card" href="/unifi-networking/">
					<span class="card-index">Network</span>
					<h3>UniFi · WiFi · Security</h3>
					<p>
						Professional WiFi, UniFi Protect cameras, network security, and high-speed wireless links for homes,
						businesses, and outbuildings.
					</p>
					<span class="card-cta">Network &amp; Security</span>
				</a>
				<a class="service-card" href="/ev-charger-installation/">
					<span class="card-index">Energy</span>
					<h3>EV charging</h3>
					<p>
						Level 2 charging designed around the property’s electrical infrastructure and the way the vehicle is
						actually driven.
					</p>
					<span class="card-cta">EV Charger Installation</span>
				</a>
				<a class="service-card" href="/smart-home-automation/">
					<span class="card-index">Automation</span>
					<h3>Lutron · Shades · Josh.ai</h3>
					<p>
						Lutron lighting, motorized shades, and Josh.ai, designed so a sophisticated house stays simple to live
						in.
					</p>
					<span class="card-cta">Smart Home Solutions</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-stone" aria-labelledby="integrated-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="integrated-heading">Infrastructure, not a pile of gadgets.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					A website, a network, a camera system, a charger, and a lighting scene fail in the same way when they are
					bought one product at a time. They never quite belong to the building, or to the person who paid for them.
				</p>
				<p>
					The work here is the layer underneath daily life and daily business: a site the company owns, a network
					that reaches the rooms and the outbuilding, cameras that record locally, charging that respects the
					panel, and lighting that recalls a scene instead of an app.
				</p>
				<p>
					Customers should own and control the technology they pay for. That idea shows up differently in each
					practice, and it is the same idea.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="web-heading">
		<div class="wrap stack">
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Digital</p>
					<h2 id="web-heading">Own your website. Not just your login.</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Business sites are built as source code and published on Cloudflare’s network. For a qualifying static
						site, that removes the traditional monthly hosting package — not the domain, email, or other services
						you may still choose to buy.
					</p>
					<p>
						You can hold the repository, see the history, and move the site later. Speed and security come from the
						architecture, not from a stack of plugins.
					</p>
					<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/website-solutions/">Website solutions</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<ComparisonTable brief />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-stone" aria-labelledby="unifi-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Network</p>
				<h2 id="unifi-heading">UniFi network &amp; security solutions</h2>
				<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Homes, offices, restaurants, workshops, and larger properties get a UniFi design: gateway, switching,
					power over Ethernet, access points, and a configuration that matches how the building is used.
				</p>
				<p>
					Guest WiFi, cameras, and ordinary computers do not have to share one flat network.
					<a href="/network-security/">Segmentation</a> is part of the plan.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="/unifi-networking/">UniFi networking</a> ·
					<a href="/wifi-design/">Professional WiFi</a>
				</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="frame">
				<img
					src="/images/network-closet.webp"
					width="1152"
					height="864"
					alt="A wall-mounted network enclosure with a switch, short patch cables, and a gateway on a plywood backboard."
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<figcaption><span>Network</span><span>Enclosure</span></figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-dark" aria-labelledby="cameras-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Security / UniFi Protect</p>
				<h2 id="cameras-heading">Your security footage. Under your control.</h2>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						UniFi Protect records on equipment at the property. There is no mandatory cloud video subscription to keep
						a useful history. Placement and coverage are planned, indoors and out, including doorbells where they help.
					</p>
					<p>
						Advanced detection capabilities depend on the selected UniFi camera and Protect hardware. Person and
						vehicle detection, smart search, and license plate recognition are features of supported equipment, not of
						every camera.
					</p>
					<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/security-cameras/">Plan your camera system</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div>
				<figure class="frame">
					<img
						src="/images/camera-eave.webp"
						width="1152"
						height="864"
						alt="A compact dark camera mounted under the wood eave of a limestone wall."
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption><span>UniFi Protect</span><span>Placement</span></figcaption>
				</figure>
				<ul class="cap-list">
					<li>Local recording</li>
					<li>Remote access</li>
					<li>AI detection*</li>
					<li>License plate recognition*</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="cap-note">*Available on supported equipment.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="wifi-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="wifi-heading">Professional WiFi &amp; network design</h2>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Adding access points does not automatically fix a building. Walls, interference, and a missing Ethernet
						run decide more than the logo on the hardware.
					</p>
					<p>
						Design covers placement, signal, channel use, backhaul, and separate networks for guests, cameras, and
						everyday devices.
					</p>
					<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/wifi-design/">Design your network</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<WifiDiagram />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-stone" aria-labelledby="bridge-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="bridge-heading">Connect buildings without trenching.</h2>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						A point-to-point wireless bridge, including 60 GHz where the path is right, can carry the main network
						to a garage, workshop, barn, guest house, or remote office.
					</p>
					<p>The far building can then run WiFi, computers, cameras, voice, and other networked equipment.</p>
					<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/wireless-bridges/">Connect your outbuilding</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<WirelessBridgeDiagram />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="ev-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Energy</p>
				<h2 id="ev-heading">Charge at home. Start every day ready to drive.</h2>
				<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Level 2 charging is substantially faster than a standard 120-volt outlet. How fast, exactly, depends on
					the vehicle, the charger, the circuit, and the electrical system — so a speed is not promised up front.
				</p>
				<p>
					The panel is evaluated before anything is mounted. Some properties already have capacity. Others need load
					management or an upgrade. Neither answer is assumed.
				</p>
				<p>
					Electrical work follows applicable code, permitting, manufacturer instructions, and licensing requirements.
				</p>
				<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/ev-charger-installation/">Plan your EV charger</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="frame">
				<img
					src="/images/ev-garage.webp"
					width="1152"
					height="864"
					alt="A wall-mounted EV charger on a plaster garage wall beside a wood-trimmed opening."
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<figcaption><span>Energy</span><span>Level 2</span></figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-warm" aria-labelledby="light-heading">
		<div class="wrap stack">
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Automation</p>
					<h2 id="light-heading">Your home should respond to how you live.</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Lutron lighting and motorized shades are specified as architecture, not as a drawer of smart bulbs.
						Scenes recall a room. Keypads work for anyone who walks in.
					</p>
					<p>
						<a href="/lutron-lighting/">Lutron lighting</a> ·
						<a href="/motorized-shades/">Motorized shades</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="frame">
				<img
					src="/images/shades-room.webp"
					width="1152"
					height="864"
					alt="A living room with large windows, lowered fabric shades, limestone, and warm architectural lighting."
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<figcaption><span>Automation</span><span>Light and shade</span></figcaption>
			</figure>
			<div class="scene-grid">
				<article>
					<h3>Good morning</h3>
					<p>Selected shades open. Lighting eases into daytime settings.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Movie</h3>
					<p>Shades lower. Lighting dims. The room is set for the screen.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Good night</h3>
					<p>Selected lights go off. Shades move to their nighttime positions.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Away</h3>
					<p>Lighting and compatible systems follow the away setting you defined.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="josh-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="josh-heading">Josh.ai home intelligence</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Josh.ai is an optional voice and app layer for homes that are already professionally integrated. It can
					bring compatible lighting, shades, climate, audio, and other systems into one place.
				</p>
				<p>Integration capabilities depend on the selected equipment and system design. It is not a universal remote for every product on the market.</p>
				<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/smart-home-automation/">Explore smart home</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-dark" aria-labelledby="plan-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="plan-heading">One home. One integrated technology plan.</h2>
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						A premium room is only as reliable as the network under it. WiFi, cameras, lighting, shades, and voice
						control should branch from infrastructure that was designed, not from a router left in a closet.
					</p>
					<p>The property is treated as one environment. Products are not installed as if they had never met.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<NetworkDiagram />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<h2 id="why-heading">Designed around ownership.</h2>
				</div>
				<p class="lede">The result should remain yours after the project is finished.</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="index-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Websites</strong>
					<p>You can own the source code, hold repository access, and move the site. No proprietary page-builder lock-in.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Networks</strong>
					<p>Documented architecture on infrastructure you control, without a subscription that the network does not need.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Security</strong>
					<p>Local recording options, video you control, and remote access that is set up on purpose.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Smart homes</strong>
					<p>A real system design, a network that can carry it, and fewer disconnected apps.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>EV charging</strong>
					<p>Capacity evaluated before installation, with the next vehicle considered while the first circuit is planned.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-stone" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="split">
				<div>
					<h2 id="process-heading">From the first conversation to a system that holds.</h2>
				</div>
				<ProcessSteps />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<ServiceArea compact />
	<FAQ items={faqs.home} intro="Short answers to the questions that usually decide a project. Each service page goes further." />
	<CTA
		title="Discuss your project."
		text="Whether the need is a website, a network, a charger, or a house that should finally work as one system."
		label="Request a Consultation"
		secondaryHref="/about/"
		secondaryLabel="About the practice"
	/>
</BaseLayout>
